        "id": 542136460,
        "iid": 3992,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "feat(auth): set default host on login to a self-managed instance",
        "description": "## Description\n\nAfter `glab auth login` succeeds for an instance other than gitlab.com, glab updates the global `host` key. Commands run outside a Git repository, such as `glab repo clone`, then reach that instance instead of gitlab.com.\n\n- If the default is still `gitlab.com` and gitlab.com has no stored credentials, glab sets `host` and prints `Default instance set to <host>`.\n- If gitlab.com has credentials, or a different default has been set, glab asks first in interactive mode. In scripted mode, it prints `glab config set --global host <host>` instead.\n- Skipped in CI and when `GITLAB_HOST`, `GITLAB_URI`, or `GL_HOST` is set. Skipped for `--job-token` logins.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nResolves #310\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- `go test ./internal/commands/auth/login/...` passes.\n- New `Test_tokenLogin_updatesDefaultHost` covers every case through the `--token` path.",
