        "id": 541969695,
        "iid": 3991,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "fix(label): show the real total in the list header",
        "description": "## Description\n\n`glab label list` passed `len(labels)` as both the count and the total in its\nheader, so the total was always the size of the current page. A project with 33\nlabels showed `Showing label 30 of 30` with the default page size, and\n`3 of 3` on page 2.\n\nThis keeps the `*gitlab.Response` returned by `ListLabels` and\n`ListGroupLabels`, and prints `resp.TotalItems` as the total. When the\nresponse carries no total (GitLab omits `X-Total` for very large result sets,\nand the existing tests mock a `nil` response), it falls back to the page count,\nwhich is the current behavior.\n\nThe table body and the JSON output are unchanged.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nResolves #8573\n\nRelated to #1165, which covers list commands that print no total at all.\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- Added a project case and a group case to\n  `internal/commands/label/list/label_list_test.go` that mock a response with\n  `TotalItems: 33`. Both fail on `main` with `2 of 2` / `1 of 1` and pass with\n  this change. The existing cases, which mock a `nil` response, still pass.\n- `go test ./internal/commands/label/...` passes.\n- `golangci-lint run ./internal/commands/label/...` (v2.14.0, as pinned in\n  `.tool-versions`) reports 0 issues, and `golangci-lint fmt --diff` reports no\n  changes.\n- `go run ./scripts/comment-overlap` reports 0 findings on the changed files.\n- Ran a build of this branch against a self-managed GitLab 19.3.3-ee project\n  with 33 labels:\n\n  | Command | `main` | This branch |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | `glab label list` | `30 of 30` | `30 of 33` |\n  | `glab label list -p 2` | `3 of 3` | `3 of 33` |\n  | `glab label list -P 10` | `10 of 10` | `10 of 33` |\n  | `glab label list -g GROUP` | `30 of 30` | `30 of 33` |\n\n  The table body and `-F json` output are byte-identical to `main`.",
        "state": "opened",
