      {
        "id": 541959514,
        "iid": 3990,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "ci(release): render Slack release notes as markdown",
        "description": "## What\n\nImproves the release announcement goreleaser posts to Slack, and tidies the release notes it generates.\n\n### Slack post\n\n- Release notes go in a Slack `markdown` block, so headings, bold text and links render instead of showing raw `##`/`###` markdown.\n- The extra `## Changelog` heading is dropped.\n- Each line ends with an emoji for the commit author type:\n  - 🤖 for `gitlab-bot@gitlab.com`\n  - `:tanuki:` for other `@gitlab.com` authors\n  - `:community:` for everyone else\n- Notes are cut at 10,000 characters and end with `…`, which keeps them under Slack's 12,000-character limit for a markdown block.\n- `message_template` is now a short plain-text fallback for notification previews.\n- `icon_emoji` is `:glab:` to match the bot's existing avatar.\n- The pre-release warning and `release.prerelease: auto` are removed. goreleaser ignores that setting for GitLab releases, and the last pre-release tag was `v1.20.0-pre1`.\n\n### Changelog lines (Slack and GitLab release page)\n\n- Author emails are dropped, and each commit SHA links to the commit.\n- The `type(scope):` prefix is bold. Messages whose prefix contains a space, such as `Revert \"…\"`, are left alone.\n- Maintenance is listed above Dependencies. The Dependencies group stays first in the config so it still claims the `chore(deps)` commits.\n- Author-type markers are written as HTML comments (`<!--team-->` etc.). GitLab doesn't display them, so the release page has no author emojis. The Slack template swaps them for the emojis.\n\nExample line:\n\n```\n* **feat(df):** add package command to check a single PURL ([c81a40c8](https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli/-/commit/c81a40c8)) by Michael Eddington :tanuki:\n```\n\n## Why\n\nThe current post sends markdown as plain Slack text, so headings show up literally and every line includes an email address. This is based on the gitlab-lsp release post.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `goreleaser check` passes.\n- Rendered the changelog format and Slack block templates against the v1.120.0 commits with a local copy of goreleaser's template functions. Also tested a `Revert \"…\"` message, a message with a second `: `, and the 10,000-character cut-off.\n- Checked with GitLab's markdown API that the HTML comment markers aren't displayed.\n- Previewed the Slack block in Block Kit Builder. Not posted to a real webhook, so the first release after merge is the end-to-end check.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
